{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00595",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 13.38,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "Good morning. Forgive me, am I right in thinking you are the doctor who deals with nerves, or have I come to the wrong room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.82,
      "end_seconds": 21.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "You're in the right place. I'm the neurologist. What's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.61,
      "end_seconds": 33.1,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Thank you. It's my legs, I'm afraid. In the evenings they become quite impossible to keep still."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.02,
      "end_seconds": 38.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Describe the feeling for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.74,
      "end_seconds": 55.26,
      "duration_seconds": 15.52,
      "text": "A sort of crawling, creeping sensation deep inside, from the knee down to the ankle. Moving is the only relief. I have to get up and walk about the kitchen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.63,
      "end_seconds": 61.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.16,
      "end_seconds": 69.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.56,
      "text": "About four months, I should say, though it has been worse since the spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.03,
      "end_seconds": 74.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "How often does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.1,
      "end_seconds": 80.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Nearly every night. Most evenings from around nine o'clock."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.12,
      "end_seconds": 87.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "And what does it do to your sleep?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.93,
      "end_seconds": 109.12,
      "duration_seconds": 19.19,
      "text": "Rather a lot, I'm afraid. I lie awake for an hour or two before I can drop off, and then I am exhausted in the daytime. I nodded off over my book only yesterday afternoon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.01,
      "end_seconds": 116.39,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Does anything make it worse, as far as you have noticed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.51,
      "end_seconds": 130.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "A strong cup of coffee after dinner, I think. I have a weakness for it. And sitting through the evening news."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.71,
      "end_seconds": 137.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Any numbness, weakness in the legs, or back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.98,
      "end_seconds": 144.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "No, none of those. Nothing of that sort at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.05,
      "end_seconds": 153.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.67,
      "text": "Right. Now, the background. Any other conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.06,
      "end_seconds": 178.94,
      "duration_seconds": 23.88,
      "text": "Well, I have high blood pressure, eight years now. And acid reflux. And arthritis in my knees, although that is more of a nuisance than anything. Oh, and migraines. I thought I had grown out of them, but I still get one once in a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.51,
      "end_seconds": 185.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Which tablets do you take for those?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.63,
      "end_seconds": 205.35,
      "duration_seconds": 17.72,
      "text": "The amlodipine, 5 milligrams every morning, for the blood pressure. And a small white tablet for the stomach acid, at night. I am so sorry, I can never remember what it is called."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.76,
      "end_seconds": 215.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Don't worry, the pharmacy list will tell us. Do you have any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.29,
      "end_seconds": 225.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Yes, penicillin. I came out in a rash all over when I was given it, years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.16,
      "end_seconds": 230.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Noted, thank you. Have you had any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.42,
      "end_seconds": 236.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "I had my gallbladder removed, about twelve years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.09,
      "end_seconds": 246.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Does anyone in your family have leg trouble like this, or other nerve conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.09,
      "end_seconds": 261.21,
      "duration_seconds": 13.12,
      "text": "My mother had restless legs, quite badly, in her seventies. And my brother has diabetes, though I don't suppose that is relevant."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.92,
      "end_seconds": 268.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Do you smoke, and how much alcohol do you drink?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.08,
      "end_seconds": 279.91,
      "duration_seconds": 9.83,
      "text": "I have never smoked. I drink a glass of wine on Saturdays, no more than that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.0,
      "end_seconds": 288.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.46,
      "text": "Right. I'd like the nurse to take your observations before I examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 291.08,
      "end_seconds": 301.25,
      "duration_seconds": 10.17,
      "text": "Of course. If you would roll up your sleeve for me. That's lovely. Blood pressure is 138/84 mmHg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 303.54,
      "end_seconds": 310.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "Pulse is 72 bpm. Temperature is 36.7 degrees Celsius, and oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 312.31,
      "end_seconds": 317.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "And you weigh 71 kilograms with your shoes off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.65,
      "end_seconds": 324.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Thank you, nurse. Mrs Okonjo-Reyes, any trouble passing water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.64,
      "end_seconds": 331.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "No, that is all quite normal, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.26,
      "end_seconds": 339.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Let me look at your legs now. Lie back on the couch for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.42,
      "end_seconds": 342.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Certainly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.11,
      "end_seconds": 355.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Reflexes are normal at the knees and ankles. Strength is normal in both legs, and there is no swelling around the ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.11,
      "end_seconds": 360.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Is that good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 361.29,
      "end_seconds": 387.7,
      "duration_seconds": 26.41,
      "text": "Yes, that's reassuring. So, here is what I think. This looks most likely to be restless legs syndrome. Your mother's history and the evening pattern both fit. I can't rule out low iron as a contributor, though, which is a common trigger, so we should check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.07,
      "end_seconds": 392.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I see. What would you suggest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.82,
      "end_seconds": 416.71,
      "duration_seconds": 22.89,
      "text": "Three things. One, a blood test for your iron stores, which I'll arrange today. Two, cut the coffee after dinner, and try a warm bath and some calf stretching before bed. Three, there are medicines for this, but I would rather not start one until the bloods are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 418.59,
      "end_seconds": 422.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Might I give up coffee entirely?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.03,
      "end_seconds": 436.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.76,
      "text": "Nothing after lunchtime would be the aim. And please bring the packet of your stomach tablet next time, so we can identify it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 438.37,
      "end_seconds": 440.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "I shall do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 443.34,
      "end_seconds": 457.44,
      "duration_seconds": 14.1,
      "text": "If the bloods are normal and your sleep is still being wrecked, I might consider a nerve conduction study, to test the nerves in your legs and be thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 459.15,
      "end_seconds": 461.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "What does that involve?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 463.67,
      "end_seconds": 470.97,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Small electrical pulses through some sticky pads. Slightly odd, but not painful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.28,
      "end_seconds": 474.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "That sounds tolerable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 476.91,
      "end_seconds": 487.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.78,
      "text": "Now, if it isn't better in six weeks, come back and see me. Sooner if the legs become weak or numb."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 489.86,
      "end_seconds": 493.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "And if the bloods show something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 495.66,
      "end_seconds": 502.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Then we treat that first, which is exactly why we do them first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 503.16,
      "end_seconds": 507.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. You have been most thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 510.2,
      "end_seconds": 519.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.04,
      "text": "Good luck with the coffee. The nurse will show you where to have the blood taken."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 521.9,
      "end_seconds": 524.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "This way, please, Mrs Okonjo-Reyes."
    }
  ]
}
